{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407270-rainbow-steel-fusing-the-5-jades","id":1407270,"title":"Rainbow Steel: Fusing the 5 Jades","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-10T04:26:59-07:00","id":1407270,"title":"Rainbow Steel: Fusing the 5 Jades","content":"My character is undertaking a personal quest to surpass his current limitations and break into Essence 4. We recently killed a circle of Dragonbloods that were each equipped with artifact jade armor and weapons. So I had an idea: My Twilight Crafter will try to fuse the 5 jades into a new material, which he is calling Rainbow Steel (working title). I want the new material to have properties better than just &quot;you can use all 5 elements like the Avatar&quot;, since its not a sword composed of just welding 5 jade types together but the creation of something new. I'm looking for some ideas for what you'd expect such a material to be able to do. <br /> <br /> here's my very brief brainstorming so far:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The fusing of the 5 jades into one new material- \u201cRainbow Steel\u201d. This isn't the same has just making a 5 sword with a whole spectrum of elemental powers, this is tying the powers of creation itself into a new essence, a material that channels the Will of Creation, the defining blade of the Terrestrial World.<br /> It will require Rainbow Steel, to do what none other has<br /> It will require Oricalcum, to give it the All-Power<br /> It will require Gossamer, that it might do the Impossible<br /> It will require Starmetal, to cheat the heavens, who would seek to interfere.<br /> - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -<br /> The Rainbow Sword (working name) represents a lot of things. In story, it proves that Salazan has grown past the teaching of Alveua and his reliance on demon summoning. It's his first step into becoming Salazan, the Wonder Maker.<br /> The star-metal is worked into small pins, and arranged to match the constellations of the Sidereals, hiding the sword from the heavens and allowing it to cheat fate. The Oricaclum is worked into hair thin strands of circuitry, connecting those constellations and amplifies/channels the reality powers of the Rainbow Steel. The Gossamer silk will be woven into the steal as it is folded and mixed, in wavelike patterns that ripple with the impossibilities and dreams of the fae, to make its abilities supersede the physical.<br /> General Evocation themes:<br /> The Rainbow Steel should offer Salazan a degree of control over the world. It is the Sword of Terrestrial Mastery. More than just blending the elements, the fusion of the 5 into something new should give Salazan a deeper connection to the magic of the actual land of Creation.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm trying to come up with some evocations and themes for the Rainbow Steel in general and the Sword in particular. My current idea is that it represents something similiar to what Gaia would make if she made a sword: not just the elements, but control over various aspects of Creation. this is Artifact 5, so dont hold back on any outlandish ideas. The Fae Gossamer and Starmetal Constellations are there more for cool flavor than anything else, but feel free to suggest any ideas. <br /> <br /> I have enough material to make the sword and a set of armor if it goes well, so if you have any armor ideas don't hesitate to throw them at me. <br /> <br /> Thank you. Sorry this is kind of half-baked, I just thought of it today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T06:29:43-07:00","id":1407285,"title":"","content":"If jade (or any other MM) could be turned into something greater just by properly mixing them together in an artifact 5 there would be a handful of Realm / Lookshy / First Age heirlooms like that.<br /> <br /> I feel this material + weapon would be inconsistent with how the setting defines its MM and how the denizens of Creation would know its history.<br /> So I'd make it N/A instead of 5. N/A gives you the opening to go balls to the wall and make something that is the stuff of legends both in effect and in how likely it'd be to exist in the first place. (The odds of making an A5 over an N/A for a db is in the &quot;counting zeroes&quot; scale)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-10-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T08:04:31-07:00","id":1407294,"title":"","content":"I agree with Synapse, in that I'd push for artifact N/A if you have the ability - if this rainbow steel fusion is a difficult enough trick that the great powers of the world haven't already developed it as a basic magical metalworking procedure, then it probably represents a seismic degree of potency.<br /> <br /> From the themes you describe, if your twilight is into wyld-shaping, this could be a fertile ground for build-offs - the ability to engage in small-scale combat-time wyldshapes to change terrain, set traps, magic up small temporary battlegroups. Alternately, a weapon that interacts with the world's geomancy, a-la Death at the Root, could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Perhaps make it a weapon embodying the nature of the elemental poles? At least as described in 2E, the closer you went to the poles, the more the wyld landscape and life became dominated by the associated element. Perhaps being able to switch the elemental nature of the weapon, granting broads buffs or debuffs to everything nearby?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:17:37-07:00","id":1407311,"title":"","content":"Fivefold Dragon's Claw from Heirs to the Shogunate might be something to look to for inspiration - it's made of the five colors of jade, though separate pieces rather than fused, and has a theme about the relationship between the elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T15:40:39-07:00","id":1407589,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts, though not done in a systematic way:<br /> <br /> Iridium might be a better name than rainbow steel. The name comes from Iris, the goddess of the rainbow in Greek myth.<br /> Other possibilities include prisma (from prism), chroma (meaning color), and Yliaster/Iliaster/Yliastrum (from greek meaning matter + star and was coined to describe primordial matter)<br /> <br /> I agree with the suggestion of N/A. Where this purely an artifact of this &quot;rainbow steel&quot; I would agree with 5, but you have brought in the heavens and other realms of being which would seem to widen its thematic scope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With that in mind, here is one way this artifact could go:<br /> <br /> Tatenen(1), the Worldseed<br /> <br /> Themes: Defying chaos, creating/manipulating landscape features/geomancy, redefining the local laws of fate/physics<br /> Evocations ideas: Create a temporary demesne at your location, upgrades to that which bring additional effects to shape the land, more creative mirrors to Death at the Root, Wyld Shaping Technique expansion that lets you shape REALLY fast by using the artifact as the &quot;seed&quot;.<br /> <br /> (1) An ancient egyptian god whose name means &quot;risen land&quot; or &quot;exalted earth&quot;. He was the personification of the primordial mound that rose from the waters from which the world was made","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T17:29:43-07:00","id":1407615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407270-rainbow-steel-fusing-the-5-jades?p=1407589#post1407589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few thoughts, though not done in a systematic way:<br /> <br /> Iridium might be a better name than rainbow steel. The name comes from Iris, the goddess of the rainbow in Greek myth.<br /> Other possibilities include prisma (from prism), chroma (meaning color), and Yliaster/Iliaster/Yliastrum (from greek meaning matter + star and was coined to describe primordial matter)<br /> <br /> I agree with the suggestion of N/A. Where this purely an artifact of this &quot;rainbow steel&quot; I would agree with 5, but you have brought in the heavens and other realms of being which would seem to widen its thematic scope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With that in mind, here is one way this artifact could go:<br /> <br /> Tatenen(1), the Worldseed<br /> <br /> Themes: Defying chaos, creating/manipulating landscape features/geomancy, redefining the local laws of fate/physics<br /> Evocations ideas: Create a temporary demesne at your location, upgrades to that which bring additional effects to shape the land, more creative mirrors to Death at the Root, Wyld Shaping Technique expansion that lets you shape REALLY fast by using the artifact as the &quot;seed&quot;.<br /> <br /> (1) An ancient egyptian god whose name means &quot;risen land&quot; or &quot;exalted earth&quot;. He was the personification of the primordial mound that rose from the waters from which the world was made</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A little sciency but Iridium is a cool name, though does this then mean Iridium in Creation is actually composed of jade? <br /> <br /> I like Polychrome as a name.<br /> <br /> But Rainbow steel sounds pretty evocative, though I would add Starmetal is a rainbow hued meteoric Iron already.<br /> <br /> Or Titanite.<br /> <br /> Or well Platinum, if only it was from the Stars then you could call it Starplatinum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T17:47:16-07:00","id":1407617,"title":"","content":"I really appreciate everyone's feedback. A few thoughts:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar894_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"894\" data-vbnamecard=\"894\">Skeptic Tank</a> : Good call about Artifact N/A. I didn't get to the brainstorming part where i come up with a reason no one has ever done it before. If it requires Celestial Circle Sorcerous Workings and it's N/A then maybe only Memnon is even capable of doing it in theory. I think my rational for why it hasn't been done in the past is that nobody cared enough to work out a way to do it, and they didn't really have a reason to try. Or maybe someone did, but most of the pieces were never recovered. Or maybe some god in Yushan is killing anyone who figures it out and hides the evidence because they fear the material will be too powerful for mortals (like Prometheus giving Fire to Humans)<br /> <br /> The Star Metal and Fae Gossamer are pretty much just there for Rule of Cool. I've always liked stories and legends of craftsmen making a weapon out of impossible things: A dream, a song, the hardness of years, a broken heart, etc (thats what the Gossamer represents). There's a trope in fables and myths that a hero does something &quot;under a blanket&quot; or similar so that the gods can't see it, that's what the Starmetal is for (I don't need Sidereals sabotaging my work). At most they will add flavor to the Evocations. <br /> <br /> Names: No matter what fancy name I choose for this material, I'm pretty sure most of Creation will just call it Rainbow Steel like they call Siderite &quot;Star Metal&quot;. Honestly, only Oricalcum averts the &quot;Noun Metal&quot; or &quot;Adjective Jade&quot; system anyway (and there's a note in AotC that most people call it Demon Gold or something)<br /> <br /> I don't have Heirs to the Shogunate so I don't know what Fivefold Dragons Claw does. Is there a place I can download it? is it free?<br /> <br /> Here's Death at the Root:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>DEATH AT THE ROOT</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Death at the Root is a moonsilver grand grimcleaver, created as a planned byproduct of a Lunar\u2019s ritual suicide after the Usurpation. The great axe can fatally sever flows of Essence as well as blood. Its wielder may use it to target the Essence in a manse, demesne or persistent spell. The player rolls (Charisma + Essence) at a difficulty of the target\u2019s rating (for manses or demesnes). Success breaks all current attunements to the manse or demesne or reduces the demesne\u2019s rating by one. Attacking a spell has a difficulty of (spell\u2019s circle + 2) and cannot affect Solar Circle spells. If successful, the spell shatters as if struck with countermagic of an equal circle. Over week-long dramatic actions, the weapon can redirect dragon lines and shape the geomantic landscape, as if performing a year\u2019s worth of geomantic engineering. A single strike, directed at a demesne\u2019s geomantic stress-point, can trigger Essence buildup. (See Chapter Two for rules about creating and destroying demesnes.)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Striking a person inflicts damage as normal. It also allows the above roll to be made reflexively. Charms or other magical effects currently affecting the target end immediately if the minimum Essence score required to use them is equal to or less than the successes rolled; effects without minimum Essence requirements compare their creator\u2019s Essence score to the number of successes instead. Attuning to Death at the Root costs eight motes. The weapon uses the normal statistics for a moonsilver grand grimcleaver, and its wielder can always channel Conviction for any roll related to Death at the Root.</span></span><br /> <i>Death at the Root guarantees a character has vast control over the magical landscape in his life. He can destroy enemies\u2019 manses permanently and end most effects that protect them. This very clearly qualifies as Artifact 5, able to completely change the face of a game no matter who holds it.</i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It cuts essence. I like that direction- the flow of Essence is a major part of Creation and it stands to reason the Captain Planet Sword could do something with that. Dragon Lines, Geomancy, cutting a spell in half. <br /> <br /> This was a hodgepodge post, sorry. I just woke up and I'm trying to shirk my IRL responsibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}